A. CREDIT TRANSFER
1. Account Verification (Send to Account).
    Request:
        The Originator bank initates Account Verification Request to IPS:
            - beneficary customer account number
            - beneficary bank.

    Response:
        IPS responds with the Account Verification Report to the Originator Bank containing:
            - beneficiary name.
    
    Action:
        Originator bank confirms with sending customer, that they are paying to the correct recipient
        Originator bank proceeds to initiate a Credit Transfer financial message.


2. Account Verification (Send to Phone).
    Request:
        The Originator Bank Initiates Account Verification Request to IPSL:
            - beneficary customer phone number.

    Response:
        IPSL lookup responds with the beneficiary details:
            - Banks that the beneficiary phone number is registered,
            - Name of beneficiary
            - Beneficiary account number.
    
    Action:
        Originator bank confirms with sending customer, that they are paying to the correct recipient
        Originator bank proceeds to initiate a Credit Transfer financial message.

3. Credit Transfer
    The Originator Bank initiates a Credit Transfer message to the IPS. 

    Action:
        I: The IPS validates the message, by performing below tasks:
            - Checks status of the Originator Bank and Beneficiary Bank,
            - Checks existing limits for the participants
            - Checks whether the Originator Bank’s net position allows performing the transaction
        II: If all the validations performed are successful, IPS forwards the Credit Transfer message to the Beneficiary Bank
            IPS starts the timeout counter (Maximum of 50 seconds)
        III: Beneficiary Bank receives the credit transfer message
             Beneficiary bank put a hold on account to be credited and responds with the positive confirmation, with the Credit Transfer Status Report message
        IV: IPS receives the response before timeout expires
            It positively validates the received response Credit Transfer Status Report message and changes net positions on the participants.

    Response From IPS
        The IPS then submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Originator Bank. 

    Action:
        Originator bank informs the customer about the successful transaction
        The IPS also submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Beneficiary Bank
        Based on this message the Beneficiary Bank credits the beneficiary customers’ account.

4. Investigative Message
    The Originator Bank initiates an investigative message If there is no final confirmation (Credit Transfer Status Report message) received from the IPS
    The Originator Bank can initiate an investigative message, before finalizing the debit transaction with its customer.

    Request:
        - Fields Not provided.

    Response:
        - credit transfer status report message
        - status of the initial credit transfer transaction


================================================================ END OF CREDIT TRANSFER ================================================================

B. PAY TO BUSINESS (PAYBILL)
1. Billers Account Verification on MGW lookup.
    Request:
        The Originator Bank initiates Biller’s Name Verification Request to IPSL lookup:
            - biller’s paybill number.

    Response: 
        - PIC code that the biller’s paybill number is registered
        - Name of biller
        - Biller’s account number.
    
    Action:
        Originator bank confirms with sending customer, that they are paying to the correct biller

2. PGW Validation.
    Request:
        The Originator Bank then proceeds to initiate the validation request to the PGW:
            - bill reference/account number
            - amount.

    Response: 
        - PGW forwards the positive confirmation response to originator bank if the validation was successful.

3. Credit Transfer
    The Originator Bank initiates a Credit Transfer message to the IPS. 

    Action:
        I: The IPS validates the message, by performing below tasks:
            - Checks status of the Originator Bank and Beneficiary Bank,
            - Checks existing limits for the participants
            - Checks whether the Originator Bank’s net position allows performing the transaction
        II: If all the validations performed are successful, IPS forwards the Credit Transfer message to the Beneficiary Bank
            IPS starts the timeout counter (Maximum of 50 seconds)
        III: Beneficiary Bank receives the credit transfer message
             Beneficiary bank put a hold on account to be credited and responds with the positive confirmation, with the Credit Transfer Status Report message
        IV: IPS receives the response before timeout expires
            It positively validates the received response Credit Transfer Status Report message and changes net positions on the participants.

    Response From IPS
        The IPS then submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Originator Bank. 

    Action:
        Originator bank informs the customer about the successful transaction
        The IPS also submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Beneficiary Bank
        Based on this message the Beneficiary Bank credits the beneficiary customers’ account.

4. Payment Confirmation Request.
    Request:
        Originator bank initiates a payment confirmation request to the PGW after receiving a successful Credit Transfer Status Report message.
            - payment confirmation request.

    Response: 
        - success status from PGW.

================================================================ END OF PAY TO BUSINESS (PAYBILL) ================================================================

c. PAY TO BUSINESS (MERCHANT - TILL)
1. Merchant’s Name Verification on MGW.
    Request:
        The  Originator Bank initiates Merchant’s Name Verification Request to IPSL lookup:
            - merchant’s till number.

    Response: 
        - PIC code of the bank that the merchant’s till is registered,
        - Name of merchant
        - Merchant’s account number.
    
    Action:
        Originator bank confirms with sending customer, that they are paying to the correct biller

2. Credit Transfer
    The Originator Bank initiates a Credit Transfer message to the IPS. 

    Action:
        I: The IPS validates the message, by performing below tasks:
            - Checks status of the Originator Bank and Beneficiary Bank,
            - Checks existing limits for the participants
            - Checks whether the Originator Bank’s net position allows performing the transaction
        II: If all the validations performed are successful, IPS forwards the Credit Transfer message to the Beneficiary Bank
            IPS starts the timeout counter (Maximum of 50 seconds)
        III: Beneficiary Bank receives the credit transfer message
             Beneficiary bank put a hold on account to be credited and responds with the positive confirmation, with the Credit Transfer Status Report message
        IV: IPS receives the response before timeout expires
            It positively validates the received response Credit Transfer Status Report message and changes net positions on the participants.

    Response From IPS
        The IPS then submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Originator Bank. 

    Action:
        Originator bank informs the customer about the successful transaction
        The IPS also submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Beneficiary Bank
        Based on this message the Beneficiary Bank credits the beneficiary customers’ account.

=========================================================== END OF PAY TO BUSINESS (MERCHANT - TILL) ===========================================================

D. REQUEST TO PAY (3rd Party PSP).
    STEPS:
        A: The Third-party PSP (Payment Service Provider) submits Customer Credit Transfer initiation message to the IPS
           The message contains data necessary for payment initiation:
                - Originator Bank name
                - Beneficiary Bank name
                - Ultimate Debtor’s name and account number 
                - Ultimate Creditor’s name and account number 
                - Payment details

        B: The IPS system validates the payment initiation message and forwards Customer Credit Transfer initiation message to the Originator Bank

        C: The Originator Bank has to communicate the request with its customer (Ultimate Debtor), and to receive approval for the Credit Transfer initiation
            If the Originator Bank’s customer (Ultimate Debtor) confirms the payment, the Originator Bank debits the customer and initiates the Credit Transfer message

        D: The IPS validates the message
            If all the validations performed are successful, IPS forwards the Credit Transfer message to the Beneficiary Bank and starts the timeout counter (Maximum of 50 seconds)

        E: Beneficiary Bank (where the PSP’s account resides) receives the credit transfer message 
            Beneficiary bank puts a hold on account to be credited and responds with the positive confirmation, with the Credit Transfer Status Report message

        F: IPS receives the response before timeout expires
            It positively validates the received response Credit Transfer Status Report message and changes net positions on the participants

                F1: The IPS then submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Originator Bank
                    Originator bank informs the customer about the successful transaction

                F2: The IPS also submits Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Beneficiary Bank
                    Based on this message the Beneficiary Bank credits the PSP’s account

        G: After the Credit Transfer is successfully processed, the IPS initiates Payment Status Report message to inform the Third-party PSP about the final           status of the initiated payment.

=========================================================== END OF REQUEST TO PAY (3rd Party PSP) ===========================================================

E. REQUEST TO PAY (WITH MANDATE).
    STEPS:
        A: The Beneficiary Bank (Initiating Participant) initiates Payment Activation Request to the Originator Bank as the Request to Pay with Mandate ID message
           The request message contains;
                - Originator Bank name
                - Beneficiary Bank name
                - Ultimate Debtor's name and account number
                - Ultimate Creditor’s name and account number
                - Payment details.
                - Mandate ID (Mandate Code)

        B: The IPS successfully validates the received message and forwards the Payment Activation Request to the Originator Bank

        C: Originator Bank performs necessary validation on the Mandate Identification (Mandate Code)
           Originator Bank confirms debit on the Ultimate Debtor’s account and responds with the Credit Transfer message
           This response message contains the Mandate ID and reference ID of the initial message

        D: The IPS validates the received message by performing below tasks;
                - Checks status of the Originator Bank and beneficiary Bank,
                - Checks existing limits for the participants,
                - Checks whether the Originator Bank’s net position allows performing the transaction

        E: If all the validations performed are successful, the IPS changes net positions on the participants

        F: IPS then submits the final Credit Transfer Status Report message to the Beneficiary Bank, informing it of the positive result of initial Request to Pay      with Mandate request.

=========================================================== END OF REQUEST TO PAY (WITH MANDATE) ===========================================================




































